## Phone (`phone` + `phone_country`)

### Implementation

- `validate_phone_number(value, country_code=...)` in [`proformas/services.py`](proformas/services.py)
- Length from `Country.phone_national_digits` for the given `country_code`
- References: [`ClientForm`](proformas/forms.py) and [`SiteForm`](proformas/forms.py) (`clean_phone`, `phone_country`, `__init__`, `clean()`)
- Templates: [`client_form.html`](templates/proformas/includes/client_form.html), [`site_form.html`](templates/proformas/includes/site_form.html)

### Validation (when provided)

1. Strip non-digits
2. Fewer than expected → `Phone has fewer than N digits.`
3. More than expected → `Phone has more than N digits.`
4. Exactly expected length → return digit string (no checksum)
5. Empty → only when phone is optional for that entity (clients and sites require phone today)

### UI pattern

- `phone_country` fk → [`countries`](proformas/models.py) table (dial code + national length)
- Selector default Portugal, **disabled** until more countries are enabled
- User types **national digits only**; template shows `+351` as visual prefix
- Store `phone` as national digits only (`max_length=9` for PT); do not store `+351` in `phone`
- Disabled `phone_country` omitted from POST — set in `clean()` from instance or default `PT` (both ClientForm and SiteForm)

### HQ site copy

On new client, [`save_client`](proformas/services.py) copies `phone_country`, `phone`, `email`, and contact fields to the auto-created HQ site. Follow the same pattern if adding other auto-copy paths.

### Checklist — new/changed phone field

- [ ] `docs/data-points.md` documents `phone_country` + national `phone`
- [ ] `clean_*` calls `validate_phone_number` with correct `country_code`
- [ ] `configure_nine_digit_form_field` on national number input
- [ ] Seed/fixtures use 9-digit national values (not `+351 …`)
